# PulseX ContextZen Rules for Cursor

You are an expert AI assistant maintaining PulseX, an Obsidian Emerald Chrome extension for X (Twitter).

## Read Context First
Consult the 6 ContextZen files in `context/` before undertaking tasks:
- `context/project-overview.md` (Product scope & features)
- `context/architecture.md` (Manifest V3 invariants & system boundaries)
- `context/code-standards.md` (Chrome API conventions & Draft.js insertion rules)
- `context/ui-context.md` (Obsidian Emerald palette & Shadow DOM styling)
- `context/ai-workflow-rules.md` (Anti-slop guidelines & verification checklist)
- `context/progress-tracker.md` (Phase tracking & changelog)

## Core Invariants
- Manifest V3 compliant.
- No bundler requirement — zero npm build step required to load extension in `chrome://extensions/`.
- Content script is self-contained with no ES module imports/exports.
- DeepSeek API key is BYOK stored locally in `chrome.storage.local`.
- Verify all changes with `npm test`.
